Z||000000||Michael||09-18-2000||10:39 PM||||Ihave a 85GT that needs some severe TLC. I get a knocking sound in the rt front wheel area when i apply brakes, doesn`t matter how hard or how soft I apply still same noise.  Wheel bearings? Steering Rack?||||reg||1
Z||000001||corsica91||09-18-2000||10:43 PM||||I have the same problem, I don't know what it is either.<P>Nathan||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||09-18-2000||11:51 PM||||I have that problem with the right rear of my 88 coupe. It sounds like the wheel is going to fall off! And as usual when dealing with a Fiero, it doesn't do it all the time.<P>At first I thought it was the CV. That was fine. A couple of my buddies helped me figure it out and it appears to be the rotor. Everyone agrees. Locally, rotors for the 88 at $100 each. I'm gonna order some soon, probably from the Fiero store. They have them for $49.95 each. Less for 84-87 models.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||09-18-2000||11:55 PM||||If you haven't had the wheel off you better. soon. just to make sure the rotor isn't cracked.<P>In addition to problems in the rotor and hub check the a arm bushings and ball joints. they can cause or at least contribute to this.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Songman||09-19-2000||12:01 AM||||Good idea, Ogre... I guess I know what I'm doing tomorrow. Thanks.||||reg||1
